{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_gameplay_input_scripting_scriptservice", "label": "ScriptService<TService> fa\u00e7ade base", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/gameplay/input-scripting.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Symmetric to ScriptComponent (static engine) with a static token resolved through the engine's ServiceRegistry \u2014 no global static, so multi-engine and testable; throws loudly at construction if the token or service is missing."}, {"id": "docs_gameplay_input_scripting_service_cached_at_ctor", "label": "Service cached at constructor (divergence from ScriptComponent)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/gameplay/input-scripting.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A service is never un-provided (ServiceRegistry has no unprovide) so the reference cannot go stale \u2014 unlike a component, whose membership is mutable and forces re-resolution. This divergence is intentional and must not be 'aligned' with ScriptComponent."}, {"id": "docs_gameplay_input_scripting_inputapi", "label": "InputApi curated fa\u00e7ade", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/gameplay/input-scripting.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Named distinctly from the backend Input interface; exposes only read-only polling (isDown/isPressed/isReleased, mousePosition/mouseDelta/scrollDelta) and never lets endFrame/clearAll/keys/pointer reach a script."}, {"id": "docs_gameplay_input_scripting_defineactions", "label": "defineActions + button()/value()/vector2() builders", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/gameplay/input-scripting.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Authoring produces a serializable data descriptor (not runtime objects) and lifts the name\u2192kind map into the type system, so map.get(\"jump\") is typed and a wrong name is a compile error \u2014 aligned with the engine's serialization/editor direction."}, {"id": "docs_gameplay_input_scripting_inputactionmap", "label": "InputActionMap runtime", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/gameplay/input-scripting.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Each action keeps current + previous so edges are correct at the ACTION level, not just the key level; that transition point is the seam where events and interactions will plug in."}, {"id": "docs_gameplay_input_scripting_buttonaction", "label": "ButtonAction", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/gameplay/input-scripting.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_gameplay_input_scripting_vector2action", "label": "Vector2Action", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/gameplay/input-scripting.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Raw composite in v1: a WASD diagonal returns (1,1), not (0.707,0.707); normalisation is deferred to an optional processor."}, {"id": "docs_gameplay_input_scripting_playerinput", "label": "PlayerInput component", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/gameplay/input-scripting.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A raw Nexus component with no fa\u00e7ade: there is no authority to route, and the action handles already ARE the curated read API \u2014 adding a third concept would be pure ceremony."}, {"id": "docs_gameplay_input_scripting_playerinputsystem", "label": "PlayerInputSystem", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/gameplay/input-scripting.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Samples at update/Early \u2014 after the DOM backend filled the frame, before scripts at Logic, and before endFrame clears edges at Late. Resolves INPUT lazily so gameplay does not declare it in requires and there is no boot coupling."}, {"id": "docs_gameplay_input_scripting_input_vocabulary", "label": "isDown / isPressed / isReleased vocabulary", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/gameplay/input-scripting.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Backend naming is kept across all three layers (backend, InputApi, actions) rather than adopting Unity's getKey*; introducing wasPressedThisFrame or redefining isPressed as held is explicitly forbidden."}, {"id": "docs_gameplay_input_scripting_persistent_action_handles", "label": "Persistent action handles mutated in place", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/gameplay/input-scripting.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Action objects live in the map and are mutated each frame, so a reference grabbed once in onCreate stays valid for the entity's lifetime \u2014 never re-created per frame or per get()."}, {"id": "docs_gameplay_input_scripting_dt_seam", "label": "dt threaded through sample()", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/gameplay/input-scripting.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Unused in v1 but passed anyway so time-based interactions (hold/tap) can be added later without changing the signature; it must not be removed 'because it is unused'."}, {"id": "docs_gameplay_input_scripting_onfixedupdate_caveat", "label": "Read input in onUpdate, not onFixedUpdate", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/gameplay/input-scripting.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Edges are per update-frame and valid at stage Logic (before endFrame at Late); in the fixed lane, which runs 0..N times per frame, they are ambiguous. Documented, with no runtime guard."}, {"id": "docs_gameplay_input_scripting_live_vec2_leak", "label": "Live mutable Vec2 returned to scripts", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/gameplay/input-scripting.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "mousePosition/mouseDelta and Vector2Action.readValue() hand back the live backend Vec2, which a script could mutate; cloning would allocate on every access every frame, so it was rejected and the risk is watched instead."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_gameplay_input_scripting_playerinputsystem", "target": "docs_core_scheduling_registersystem", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/gameplay/input-scripting.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_gameplay_input_scripting_onfixedupdate_caveat", "target": "docs_core_scheduling_stage_vocabulary", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/gameplay/input-scripting.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_gameplay_input_scripting_inputapi", "target": "docs_gameplay_input_scripting_scriptservice", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/gameplay/input-scripting.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_gameplay_input_scripting_service_cached_at_ctor", "target": "docs_gameplay_input_scripting_scriptservice", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/gameplay/input-scripting.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_gameplay_input_scripting_s